    "title": "If TDF stopped, substitute per guideline",
    "message": "Guidelines specify that for moderate and severe adverse reactions, the responsible ARV should be substituted following specific substitution guidance. For TDF toxicity, the guideline substitution is AZT if TDF is contraindicated. If the clinician proceeds with permanent TDF discontinuation, the plan should include a specific substitute ARV rather than simply stopping TDF, to maintain viral suppression. The patient is currently virally suppressed (<50 copies/mL), and an unstructured regimen change risks treatment interruption or resistance.",
