    "alert_id": "EX2_AKI_SEVERITY_MONITORING",
    "title": "Severe creatinine rise requires close monitoring",
    "message": "Guideline toxicity grading defines severe renal dysfunction as eGFR 30 to <60 mL/min or a 30 to <50% decrease from baseline. This patient's creatinine rose from 0.9 to 2.4 mg/dL, a substantial acute decline in renal function meeting severe toxicity criteria. Guidelines recommend renal function tests (RFTs) when TDF-related toxicity is suspected, and serum creatinine monitoring is part of routine TDF safety monitoring. The plan includes fluid resuscitation but does not document repeat creatinine/eGFR monitoring or a defined threshold for ART adjustment.",
